ifference 5, starting at a, then a=98.57, leading to angles 98.57,103.57, ..., up to a +5*6≈98.57 +30≈128.57. Sum=7*98.57 +75= around 765, but polygon requires 945. Thus, inconsistency. So arithmetic progression with difference 5 and starting at a=(180(n-2) -5n(n-1)/2)/n gives a different sum.\n\nBut here\'s the issue. The formula for a is derived from the fact that the angles are in arithmetic progression with difference 5. However, in reality, for a convex polygon, the interior angles must not only be in arithmetic progression with difference 5 but also their sum must equal (n-2)*180. Therefore, solving these two conditions:\n\n1. Sum: n a +5n(n-1)/2=180(n-2)\n\n2. Largest angle: a +5(n-1) <180\n\nBut these two equations involve a and n, and solving them yields the possible n.\n\nBut from equation 1:\n\na= [180(n-2) -5n(n-1)/2 ] /n\n\nSubstitute into equation 2:\n\n[180(n-2) -5n(n-1)/2 ] /n +5(n-1) <180\n\nSimplify this inequality.\n\nMultiply through by 2n to eliminate denominators:\n\n2[180(n-2) -5n(n-1)/2] +10n(n-1) <360n\n\nWhich simplifies to:\n\n360(n-2) -5n(n-1) +10n(n-1) <360n\n\nSimplify left side:\n\n360n -720 -5n^2 +5n +10n^2 -10n\n\n=360n -720 +5n^2 -5n\n\nCombine like terms:\n\n5n^2 +355n -720 <360n\n\nMove all terms to left:\n\n5n^2 +355n -720 -360n <0\n\nWhich is:\n\n5n^2 -5n -720 <0\n\nDivide through by common factor if any or simplify:\n\nn^2 -n -144 <0\n\nSolve n^2 -n -144=0:\n\nn=(1 ±√(1 +576))/2=(1 ±√577)/2≈(1 ±24.04)/2\n\nPositive root≈(25.04)/2≈12.52\n\nThus, n^2 -n -144 <0 when n<12.52. Therefore, maximum integer n=12.\n\nWait, this contradicts earlier result. So solving the inequality gives n=12 as maximum. However, let\'s test n=12.\n\nCompute a=(180*(12-2) -5*12*(12-1))/12=(180*10 -5*12*11)/12=(1800 -660)/12=1140/12=95\n\nLargest angle=95+5*(11)=95+55=150 <180, which is ok. Then angles are 95,100,...,150. Sum:\n\nSum=12*95 +5*12*11/2=1140 +5*6*11=1140 +330=1470\n\nBut (12-2)*180=1800. So 1470 is not equal to 1800. Therefore, inconsistency